window.QB_MATHS_DE = {"subject":"DP Mathematics: Analysis and Approaches","level":"HL","topic":{"number":5,"title":"First order differential equations"},"exercises":[{"id":"19N.3.AHL.TZ0.HCA_4","section":"A","paper":2,"session":"19N","date":"November 2019","tz":"TZ0","legacy":"HCA_","marks":16,"contexts":[{"id":"c0","html":"<p>Consider the differential equation <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>, with <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> when <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>.</p>"}],"parts":[{"label":"a","type":"question","marks":5,"ctx":["c0"],"q":"<p>Use Euler’s method, with step length <math><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></math>, to find an approximate value of <math><mi>y</mi></math> when <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.4</mn></math>.</p>","er":"","ms":"<img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\">"},{"label":"b.i","type":"question","marks":1,"ctx":["c0"],"q":"<p>Express <math><msup><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math> in the form <math><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></math>, where <math><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℤ</mi></math>.</p>","er":"","ms":"<img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\">"},{"label":"b.ii","type":"question","marks":10,"ctx":["c0"],"q":"<p>Solve the differential equation, for <math><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, giving your answer in the form <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>","er":"","ms":"<img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\"><img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\">"}],"notes":[]},{"id":"21M.2.AHL.TZ1.12","section":"A","paper":2,"session":"21M","date":"May 2021","tz":"TZ1","legacy":"","marks":14,"contexts":[{"id":"c0","html":"<p>The function <math><mi>f</mi></math> has a derivative given by <math><mi>f</mi><mo lspace=\"0\" rspace=\"0\">′</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></math>, <math><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℝ</mi></math>, <math><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, <math><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></math>, where <math><mi>k</mi></math> is a positive constant.</p>"},{"id":"c2","html":"<p>Consider <math><mi>P</mi></math>, the population of a colony of ants, which has an initial value of <math><mn>1200</mn></math>.</p><p>The rate of change of the population can be modelled by the differential equation <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>, where <math><mi>t</mi></math> is the time measured in days, <math><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, and <math><mi>k</mi></math> is the upper bound for the population.</p>"}],"parts":[{"label":"a","type":"question","marks":3,"ctx":["c0"],"q":"<p>The expression for <math><mi>f</mi><mo lspace=\"0\" rspace=\"0\">′</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> can be written in the form <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>, where <math><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℝ</mi></math>. Find <math><mi>a</mi></math> and <math><mi>b</mi></math> in terms of <math><mi>k</mi></math>.</p>","er":"","ms":"<img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\"><img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\">"},{"label":"b","type":"question","marks":3,"ctx":["c0"],"q":"<p>Hence, find an expression for <math><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>","er":"","ms":"<img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\">"},{"label":"c","type":"question","marks":8,"ctx":["c0","c2"],"q":"<p>By solving the differential equation, show that <math><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1200</mn><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1200</mn><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1200</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p>","er":"","ms":"<img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\">"}],"notes":[]},{"id":"EXN.2.AHL.TZ0.12","section":"A","paper":2,"session":"EXN","date":"November Example questions","tz":"TZ0","legacy":"","marks":12,"contexts":[{"id":"c0","html":"<p>Consider the differential equation <p class=\"center\"><math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"true\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.4em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>The curve <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> for <math><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math> has a gradient function given by <p class=\"center\"><math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></p>The curve passes through the point <math><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace=\"0\" rspace=\"0\">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>"}],"parts":[{"label":"a","type":"question","marks":3,"ctx":["c0"],"q":"<p>Use the substitution <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></math> to show that <math><mo>∫</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ln</mi><mo lspace=\"0\" rspace=\"0.1em\">&#x2061;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></math>, where <math><mi>C</mi></math> is an arbitrary constant.</p>","er":"","ms":"<img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\">"},{"label":"b","type":"question","marks":9,"ctx":["c0"],"q":"<p>By using the result from part (a) or otherwise, solve the differential equation and hence show that the curve has equation <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi><mo lspace=\"0\" rspace=\"0.1em\">&#x2061;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ln</mi><mo lspace=\"0\" rspace=\"0.1em\">&#x2061;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></math>.</p>","er":"","ms":"<img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\">"}],"notes":[]},{"id":"17N.3.AHL.TZ0.HCA_2","section":"A","paper":2,"session":"17N","date":"November 2017","tz":"TZ0","legacy":"HCA_","marks":10,"contexts":[{"id":"c0","html":"<p>Consider the differential equation <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math>, where <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> when <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p>"}],"parts":[{"label":"a","type":"question","marks":4,"ctx":["c0"],"q":"<p>Show that <math><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></math> is an integrating factor for this differential equation.</p>","er":"","ms":"<img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\"><img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\">"},{"label":"b","type":"question","marks":6,"ctx":["c0"],"q":"<p>Solve the differential equation giving your answer in the form <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>","er":"","ms":"<img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\">"}],"notes":[]},{"id":"18M.3.AHL.TZ0.HCA_5","section":"A","paper":2,"session":"18M","date":"May 2018","tz":"TZ0","legacy":"HCA_","marks":8,"contexts":[{"id":"c0","html":"<p>Consider the differential equation <math><mi>x</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, where <math><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℝ</mi></math>, <math><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math><mi>p</mi></math> is a positive integer, <math><mi>p</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>.</p>"}],"parts":[{"label":"","type":"question","marks":8,"ctx":["c0"],"q":"<p>Solve the differential equation given that <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo lspace=\"0\" rspace=\"0\">−</mo><mn>1</mn></math> when <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Give your answer in the form <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>","er":"","ms":"<img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\"><img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\"><img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\">"}],"notes":[]},{"id":"18N.3.AHL.TZ0.HCA_4","section":"A","paper":2,"session":"18N","date":"November 2018","tz":"TZ0","legacy":"HCA_","marks":10,"contexts":[{"id":"c0","html":"<p>Consider the differential equation <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>, where <math><mi>x</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p>"}],"parts":[{"label":"a","type":"question","marks":4,"ctx":["c0"],"q":"<p>Given that <math><mi>y</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, use Euler’s method with step length <math><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.25</mn></math> to find an approximation for <math><mi>y</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. Give your answer to two significant figures.</p>","er":"","ms":"<img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\"><img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\">"},{"label":"b","type":"question","marks":6,"ctx":["c0"],"q":"<p>Solve the equation <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> for <math><mi>y</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>.</p>","er":"","ms":"<img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\">"}],"notes":[]},{"id":"17M.3.AHL.TZ0.HCA_4","section":"A","paper":2,"session":"17M","date":"May 2017","tz":"TZ0","legacy":"HCA_","marks":13,"contexts":[{"id":"c0","html":"<p>Consider the differential equation <p class=\"center\"><math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"true\">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.4em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p></p>"}],"parts":[{"label":"a","type":"question","marks":3,"ctx":["c0"],"q":"<p>Use the substitution <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></math> to show that the general solution of this differential equation is <p class=\"center\"><math><mo>∫</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ln</mi><mo lspace=\"0\" rspace=\"0.1em\">&#x2061;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mtext>constant</mtext><mo>.</mo></math></p></p>","er":"","ms":"<img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\">"},{"label":"b","type":"question","marks":10,"ctx":["c0"],"q":"<p>Hence, or otherwise, solve the differential equation <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>, <math><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, given that <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> when <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Give your answer in the form <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>","er":"","ms":"<img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\">"}],"notes":[]},{"id":"16N.3.AHL.TZ0.HCA_1","section":"A","paper":2,"session":"16N","date":"November 2016","tz":"TZ0","legacy":"HCA_","marks":11,"contexts":[{"id":"c0","html":"<p>Consider the differential equation <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"true\">)</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>, given that <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> when <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p>"}],"parts":[{"label":"a","type":"question","marks":5,"ctx":["c0"],"q":"<p>Show that <math><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> is an integrating factor for this differential equation.</p>","er":"","ms":"<img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\">"},{"label":"b","type":"question","marks":6,"ctx":["c0"],"q":"<p>Hence solve this differential equation. Give the answer in the form <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>","er":"","ms":"<img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\">"}],"notes":[]},{"id":"19M.3.AHL.TZ0.HCA_5","section":"A","paper":2,"session":"19M","date":"May 2019","tz":"TZ0","legacy":"HCA_","marks":11,"contexts":[{"id":"c0","html":"<p>Consider the differential equation <math><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>, where <math><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p>"}],"parts":[{"label":"","type":"question","marks":11,"ctx":["c0"],"q":"<p>Solve the differential equation and show that a general solution is <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>x</mi></math> where <math><mi>c</mi></math> is a positive constant.</p>","er":"","ms":"<img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\"><img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\">"}],"notes":[]},{"id":"20N.3.AHL.TZ0.HCA_3","section":"A","paper":2,"session":"20N","date":"November 2020","tz":"TZ0","legacy":"HCA_","marks":8,"contexts":[{"id":"c0","html":"<p>The curve <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> has a gradient function given by <p class=\"center\"><math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p>The curve passes through the point <math><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>"}],"parts":[{"label":"","type":"question","marks":8,"ctx":["c0"],"q":"<p>Find the solution of the differential equation <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></math> which passes through the point <math><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. Give your answer in the form <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>","er":"","ms":"<img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\">"}],"notes":[]},{"id":"20N.2.AHL.TZ0.F_9","section":"A","paper":2,"session":"20N","date":"November 2020","tz":"TZ0","legacy":"F_","marks":9,"contexts":[{"id":"c0","html":"<p>Consider the differential equation <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>, where <math><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p><p>It is given that <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> when <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>.</p>"}],"parts":[{"label":"","type":"question","marks":9,"ctx":["c0"],"q":"<p>Solve the differential equation, giving your answer in the form <math><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p>","er":"","ms":"<img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\"><img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\">"}],"notes":[]},{"id":"22M.2.AHL.TZ1.12","section":"A","paper":2,"session":"22M","date":"May 2022","tz":"TZ1","legacy":"","marks":17,"contexts":[{"id":"c0","html":"<p>Consider the differential equation <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> for <math><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math><mi>y</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></math>. It is given that <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math> when <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>.</p>"}],"parts":[{"label":"a","type":"question","marks":4,"ctx":["c0"],"q":"<p>Use Euler’s method, with a step length of <math><mn>0.1</mn></math>, to find an approximate value of <math><mi>y</mi></math> when <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.5</mn></math>.</p>","er":"","ms":"<img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\">"},{"label":"b","type":"question","marks":3,"ctx":["c0"],"q":"<p>Use the substitution <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></math> to show that <math><mi>x</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p>","er":"","ms":"<img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\">"},{"label":"c","type":"question","marks":10,"ctx":["c0"],"q":"<p>By solving the differential equation, show that <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p>","er":"","ms":"<img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\"><img class=\"ms-crop\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" alt=\"Markscheme\">"}],"notes":[]}]};
